{
  "concept": "A string fixed at both ends can only vibrate in normal modes whose wavelength packs an exact integer number of half-wavelengths into the length L, giving the quantized relation lambda_n = 2L/n.",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "top reference line between two black endpoint dots, each labeled 'Node'",
    "double-headed dimension arrow above the reference line labeled 'L'",
    "active standing-wave envelope: dark blue curve plus pale mirror-image curve outlining the sweep",
    "left mode label 'n = k' for the selected mode",
    "black endpoint node dots on the active wave (always fixed)",
    "interior node dots on the center line (count = n - 1)",
    "right-side wavelength condition, e.g. 'k/2 * lambda_k = L'",
    "right-side solved wavelength, e.g. 'lambda_k = 2/k * L'",
    "general formula 'lambda_n = (2/n) L,  n = 1, 2, 3, ...' at lower right",
    "horizontal center (equilibrium) line through the wave"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "modeStep",
      "type": "button",
      "label": "Mode number n",
      "states": ["n = 1", "n = 2", "n = 3", "n = 4"],
      "default": "n = 1",
      "teaches": "Stepping n adds one half-wavelength inside the same fixed length L: the envelope gains one more loop and one more interior node, and the right-hand equation updates to n/2 * lambda_n = L, making the integer-fit condition explicit"
    },
    {
      "id": "oscillate",
      "type": "animation",
      "label": "Oscillate this mode",
      "loop": true,
      "teaches": "Playing the motion shows the string sweeping between the two envelope curves while the endpoint and interior nodes never move and the antinodes swing through maximum amplitude — clarifying the difference between a node (zero displacement always) and an antinode (maximum displacement)"
    },
    {
      "id": "lengthL",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "String length L",
      "range": [1, 4, 0.1],
      "default": 2,
      "teaches": "Dragging the endpoint separation stretches or contracts the whole pattern for the selected mode, and the displayed wavelength lambda_n = 2L/n scales in direct proportion to L, showing that L sets the absolute wavelength while n sets how many half-waves fit"
    }
  ],
  "demo_steps": [
    {
      "title": "Fundamental mode",
      "narration": "For n = 1 exactly one half-wavelength fits between the pinned ends, so (1/2) lambda_1 = L and lambda_1 = 2L. The two envelope curves show the full sweep; the ends are the only nodes.",
      "state": { "modeStep": "n = 1", "lengthL": 2 }
    },
    {
      "title": "Add half-wavelengths",
      "narration": "Step to n = 2, then n = 3 and n = 4: each step packs one more half-wavelength into the same L, adding one interior node and one more loop, with the right-hand equation tracking n/2 * lambda_n = L.",
      "state": { "modeStep": "n = 3", "lengthL": 2 }
    },
    {
      "title": "Nodes vs antinodes",
      "narration": "Press play: the string oscillates between the envelope curves. Watch that every node (endpoints and interior crossings) stays perfectly still while the antinodes at the loop peaks swing widest.",
      "state": { "modeStep": "n = 3", "lengthL": 2 }
    },
    {
      "title": "Length sets the wavelength",
      "narration": "Drag the L slider: the pattern and its quoted wavelength lambda_n = 2L/n stretch or shrink together, confirming that the fixed length L, not the mode number alone, fixes the actual wavelength.",
      "state": { "modeStep": "n = 2", "lengthL": 3.4 }
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "Because both ends are pinned nodes, only wavelengths that fit an exact integer number of half-wavelengths into L are allowed, quantizing the standing waves to lambda_n = 2L/n.",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Lay out a single active mode panel rather than four stacked rows, since the mode stepper replaces the stack: top shows the reference line with two black 'Node' dots and a double-headed arrow labeled L; below it the active wave drawn as a solid dark-blue sine-half-loop curve with a pale light-blue mirror image forming the envelope, ends pinned at black dots and interior nodes as small dots on a thin horizontal equilibrium line. Left of the wave put 'n = k'; right put the two equations 'k/2 * lambda_k = L' and 'lambda_k = 2/k * L' in italic serif math styling; keep the general 'lambda_n = (2/n) L,  n = 1, 2, 3, ...' pinned at lower right at all times. Use a clear blue for the live curve and a desaturated pale blue for the mirror envelope so the sweep region reads as one shape. When oscillating, animate the live curve's amplitude between the two envelopes while node dots remain fixed. Optionally render the other three modes as faint grey thumbnails down the left margin for orientation, but keep the active mode visually dominant."
}

