CONCEPT: A string fixed at both ends supports only normal modes whose wavelength packs an exact integer number of half-wavelengths into length L, giving lambda_n = 2L/n; higher n means shorter wavelength and more nodes.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): Because both ends are pinned nodes, only wavelengths satisfying (n/2)λ_n = L are allowed — stacking all four modes side by side makes the shrinking wavelength and growing node count immediately visible.
DEMO STEPS: 4 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

